//! The `baseline-source` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property defines
//! which
//! [baseline](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Values/baseline-position)
//! to use when inline-level boxes have multiple possible baselines, such as multi-line [inline
//! blocks](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Display/Block_and_inline_layout)
//! or inline [flex
//! containers](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Flexible_box_layout/Basic_concepts#the_flex_container).
//! The values allow for choosing between aligning to the box's first baseline, last baseline, or
//! letting the browser decide automatically based on the box type.
//!
//! Initial: auto. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Keyword effects:
//! - auto: Specifies [`last
//! baseline`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Values/baseline-position#last_baseline)
//! alignment for inline-block, [`first
//! baseline`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Values/baseline-position#first_baseline)
//! alignment for everything else.
//! - first: Specifies `first baseline` alignment.
//! - last: Specifies `last baseline` alignment.
//!
//! Grammar: auto | first | last
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-inline-3/#propdef-baseline-source
//!
//! Author guide:
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/baseline-source
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

